---
import BaseLayout from '../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import { SITE } from '../../lib/site';
---

<BaseLayout
  title="Privacy Policy | Toolland"
  description="How Toolland treats your files and data: processed on your device, never stored, no tracking cookies, and no ads."
  alternates={{ id: '/kebijakan-privasi', en: '/en/privacy' }}
>
  <div class="prose-tool">
    <h1 class="text-3xl font-extrabold tracking-tight text-slate-900 dark:text-slate-100">
      Privacy Policy
    </h1>
    <p class="mt-3 text-lg">
      In short: your files are never stored. Almost every tool processes files directly on your
      device, and Toolland uses no tracking cookies, ads, or accounts.
    </p>

    <h2>Tools that run on your device</h2>
    <p>
      Tools marked <strong>“Processed on your device”</strong> work entirely in your browser using
      JavaScript and WebAssembly. Files are read from your device, processed in browser memory, and
      the result is downloaded directly. Files are not sent to Toolland’s servers or anyone else.
      When you close the tab, everything is gone from memory.
    </p>

    <h2>Tools that use the server</h2>
    <p>
      A few tools, such as Word to PDF and maximum PDF compression, need a server. They are marked
      <strong>“Processed on server, deleted automatically”</strong>. For these tools:
    </p>
    <ul>
      <li>Files are sent over an encrypted connection (HTTPS), up to 15 MB.</li>
      <li>Files are kept only in server RAM (tmpfs), never written to disk or a database.</li>
      <li>
        Files and results are deleted as soon as the result is sent to you, including when an error
        occurs.
      </li>
      <li>There is no history and no link to reopen results.</li>
    </ul>

    <h2>WHOIS lookup</h2>
    <p>
      The WHOIS lookup tool sends the domain name you type to the Toolland server, which asks the
      official RDAP server of that domain's registry (for example Verisign for .com or PANDI for
      .id). Domain names are not written to the logs. Results are kept in server RAM for at most 1
      hour so the registry is not asked again and again, then deleted. Only data the registry
      already publishes is shown.
    </p>

    <h2>Subdomain Finder</h2>
    <p>
      The Subdomain Finder does not use the Toolland server. Your browser sends the domain name you
      type directly to crt.sh (run by Sectigo), or to Certspotter (run by SSLMate) when crt.sh is
      not responding, to read public SSL certificate logs. Those services see the domain name and
      your IP address, just as when you visit their sites. Toolland never receives or stores the
      domains you search.
    </p>

    <h2>Server logs</h2>
    <p>
      The server only records technical data needed to keep the service running: time, method, page
      address without parameters, status, size, and duration. File names, file contents, and full IP
      addresses are not recorded. Logs are deleted automatically after 7 days.
    </p>

    <h2>Cloudflare</h2>
    <p>
      Toolland uses Cloudflare as a CDN and security layer. Like every CDN, Cloudflare processes IP
      addresses and technical request data to deliver pages and block attacks. Toolland only sees
      aggregate visit statistics in the Cloudflare dashboard, with no tracking script on the pages.
    </p>
    <p>
      Cloudflare’s privacy policy:
      <a href="https://www.cloudflare.com/privacypolicy/" rel="noopener">
        cloudflare.com/privacypolicy
      </a>
    </p>

    <h2>Cookies and browser storage</h2>
    <p>
      Toolland uses no cookies. The only data stored in your browser is a sessionStorage flag so the
      donation card appears at most once per session, plus cached AI models and codecs so tools load
      faster next time. The flag is cleared when you close the tab. The Subdomain Finder also keeps
      the times of your searches from the last hour in localStorage to count the 10 searches per
      hour quota; it holds only timestamps, never domain names.
    </p>

    <h2>Ads and third parties</h2>
    <p>No ads, no tracking scripts, and no data is sold or shared.</p>

    <h2>Open source</h2>
    <p>
      All of Toolland’s code is open on <a href={SITE.repo}>GitHub</a> (AGPL-3.0 license), so anyone
      can verify that files are processed exactly as described here.
    </p>

    <h2>Contact</h2>
    <p>
      Privacy questions or security reports can be sent through the
      <a href={`${SITE.repo}/security`}>Security page on GitHub</a>.
    </p>
    <p class="text-sm">Last updated: November 6, 2026.</p>
  </div>
</BaseLayout>
